      "body": "### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.6.1 stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.1.stable - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 9070 XT (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 32.0.23033.1002) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-14900K (32 threads) - 63.72 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen exporting a meshlibrary from  MeshInstance3D scene, while importing in a GridMap meshlibrary, no meshes are present:\n\n<img width=\"1917\" height=\"1028\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/60dc44a2-61f2-4b25-be9f-83691a669e79\" />\n\n<img width=\"1913\" height=\"1001\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0619ee17-6de1-4c7d-b862-3bbfa6b251a3\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create a MeshInstance3D with staticBody3D and CollisionShape3D\n- Scene -> Export As ... -> MeshLibrary\n- In a scene, make a GridMap and import the .tres meshlibrary file\n- No meshes are present in the meshlibrary\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A",
